# A first example. Alice can lend Bob money, which Bob can use to make a profit. The honest play: Alice lends,
# and Bob pays the money back with interest. But nothing stops Bob from keeping it; run CheckMate to see what
# that means, and loan_with_deposit.rules for a fix.
players: Alice  # has money to lend
players: Bob    # needs money for a business
constants: loan      # what Alice lends Bob
constants: interest  # what Bob pays on top when he repays
constants: profit    # what Bob makes with the money
initial: loan > 0
initial: interest > 0
initial: profit > interest

start: Alice

honest move lend by Alice
  next Bob

move refuse by Alice  # nobody gains or loses anything
  end

honest move repay by Bob  # pays the loan back, with interest
  pay Alice: interest, Bob: profit - interest
  end

move keep by Bob  # keeps the money
  pay Alice: -loan, Bob: profit + loan
  end
